There's a stinking _lot_ of tools out there, was the
idea to cover them all? From the tools_343 spoiler,
truncated, with a couple of ideas filled in by me:

Containers
  sack
  large box
  chest
      A chest might summon a ghost, their haunting
      is often tied morbidly to objects kept in
      chests.
  ice box
      Ice troll?
  bag of holding
      owl bear, for the pun
  bag of tricks
  oilskin sack
Unlocking tools
  credit card
  lock pick
  skeleton key
      A key might summon a gnome, known for
      craftiness in manufacturing tasks working at
      small dimensions, like lock making.
Light sources
  tallow candle
  wax candle
      killer bee or queen killer bee
  brass lantern
      Brass lanterns are electric, perhaps an energy
      vortex for its shocking attack.
  oil lamp
  magic lamp
      A magic lamp should summon a hostile
      djinni/genie.
  Candelabrum of Invocation
Instruments
  tin whistle
      dog
  magic whistle
      large dog
  bugle
      soldier
  wooden flute
      Since flutes have long been linked to snake
      charming, an obvious choice for them to summon
      is snakes. Perhaps a random member of the snake
      class?
  magic flute
  tooled horn
  frost horn
  fire horn
  horn of plenty
  leather drum
      rothes, since the drum might be covered in
      rothe hide
  drum of earthquake
  wooden harp
      Harps might summon leprechauns, since the Irish used
      to carry harps into battle, or nymphs, known lovers
      of music.
  magic harp
  bell
  Bell of Opening
Traps
  beartrap
      owl bear, for the obvious pun
  land mine
      sergeant
Weapon-Tools
  pick-axe
      Pickaxes could summon dwarves, rock moles, or
      trolls (mythically some trolls _eat_ rocks).
  grappling hook
      stone gargoyle, for also being associated with
      tops of walls over which grappling hooks are
      often thrown
  unicorn horn
      unicorn, but this seems subject to abuse
Other tools
  expensive camera
  mirror
      nymph
  crystal ball
      lich
  lenses
      giant beetle, for its multi-lensed eyes
  blindfold
  towel
      keystone kop with cream pie cocked and ready.
  saddle
      pony
  leash
      small dog
  stethoscope
      A stethoscope should perhaps summon bats,
      known for sharp hearing.
  tinning kit
      quantum mechanic, for the pun of transmuting
      some other metal to tin
  tin opener
      rust monster
  can of grease
  figurine
      umber hulk or earth elemental for its rock
      penetrating capability
  magic marker

I'm sure others can add to this list. To be kind
to the OP, why not copy it whole and interpolate
your additions.

